WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.893 --> 00:00:09.292
HQ, Ask HQ and reporting. An assistant that lives inside your numbers, and the scorecards you manage by.

2
00:00:10.195 --> 00:00:17.940
Ask HQ reads the same rows your managers do. What sold yesterday, how old was it, how many leads did each get, and what did we make.

3
00:00:18.843 --> 00:00:26.723
It answers with a table you can check, then turns it into the next action. Add the finds to the buying board, text the dealers, show the comps.

4
00:00:27.625 --> 00:00:34.506
Ask which ads are working and it reads spend to conversations to approvals to deals, per campaign, and tells you which one to kill.

5
00:00:35.407 --> 00:00:41.882
Ask how to price an aged unit and it brings the comps, your cost basis and three moves with the days to sell for each.

6
00:00:42.783 --> 00:00:54.259
Everything Ask HQ can see is on the reports. Sales, service, buying, ads and chat, with the goal and the pace beside every figure, per rep and per campaign.

7
00:00:55.160 --> 00:01:02.388
The finds Ask HQ added are already on the buying board. One database, so the answer and the work are the same thing.

8
00:01:03.289 --> 00:01:12.311
And it is your data. Every table exported nightly, a read API for your own tools, an audit trail on every change, and no exit fees.

9
00:01:13.212 --> 00:01:16.749
Ask HQ, reporting and your data, in HQ.
